# Code owners — GitHub requests review from these owners on matching changes.
#
# CURRENT STATE (user-owned pilot repo):
#   - This repo is owned by a USER account (sfernandez-uala), so only individual
#     collaborators (e.g. @sfernandez-uala) are valid owners. An @org/team
#     reference is silently ignored on a user repo — it would fail OPEN, giving
#     no protection. Teams only work on ORG-owned repos.
#   - The code-owner gate is currently OFF (require_code_owner_reviews = false on
#     dev/uat/main; required_approving_review_count = 0) — deferred to the cutover.
#
# IMPACT if the gate were enabled here as-is:
#   - Bus factor = 1: @sfernandez-uala is the only designated reviewer.
#   - A user CANNOT approve their own PR. In a solo pilot the owner authors every
#     PR, so enabling "Require review from Code Owners" (+ required approvals >= 1)
#     would DEADLOCK every PR. This is why the gate stays off during the pilot.
#
# MIGRATION CHECKLIST (org cutover):
#   1. Move the repo under the target org.
#   2. Repoint the rules below from @sfernandez-uala to a real team
#      (e.g. @<org>/salesforce-platform).
#   3. THEN enable branch protection: require_code_owner_reviews = true and
#      required_approving_review_count >= 1. A team owner lets any member other
#      than the author satisfy the gate → real 4-eyes review, no deadlock.

